{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/954684-psions-had-another-idea","id":954684,"title":"Psions: Had another idea...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-20T16:53:02-07:00","id":954684,"title":"Psions: Had another idea...","content":"What if the psions gained Enhancement bonuses from working together? Singly, they do not pose a threat to most Aberrants, but with numbers of them pulling together on a single effect, suddenly they can unleash hell's full fury. Bonus points if they can get Enhancement bonuses based on the variety of psions involved.<br /> <br /> This gives them the theme of collective action, which for psychic-based characters, works really well. Now, trying to get them to work together in the first place, there's the rub. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:16:22-07:00","id":955067,"title":"","content":"Anyone? Bueller?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T16:24:07-07:00","id":955271,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a great idea, especially for psions who fight Aberrants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T17:10:39-07:00","id":955304,"title":"","content":"I jsut remember that, when Aeon/Trinity first came out, there was fluff fiction which said that psions working together were more powerful, and that psi and quanta canceled out allowing a much more equal footing between them in combat. I figured that, by getting Enhancements from working together, they could boost the psions' powers and not have to cut back on Aberrants/Novas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T09:45:04-07:00","id":957022,"title":"","content":"In the 1st edition of Aeon/Trinity there were some collaborative powers explained on Psi Coordination on page 51 in Aurora Australis for the Legions. So some of the idea made its way into mechanics, although not comprehensively.","signature":"<hr class=\"